# ---- API base URL ----
# Base URL of the Django/DRF backend. REQUIRED — this app serves no API routes
# of its own, so leaving it empty makes every request hit localhost:3000/api/*
# and 404, including login.
#
# It is also read at build time by src/proxy.ts to name the API origin in the
# Content Security Policy. If it is wrong or missing, the browser blocks every
# request to the backend and every product image, and the store renders empty
# with CSP violations in the console. That is the first thing to check if the
# catalogue will not load.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# ---- Media base URL ----
# Where product and category images are read from. OPTIONAL, and unset it falls
# back to NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL — which is correct while the backend runs
# UPLOAD_BACKEND=local and Django serves /uploads itself.
#
# Set it once images live in Cloudflare R2: the bucket's public base, either its
# r2.dev subdomain or a custom domain. The backend calls the same value
# R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL, and the two must agree — the API stores relative paths
# ("/uploads/x.png") and this is what puts a host in front of them.
#
# Read at build time by src/proxy.ts to name the origin in the CSP's `img-src`,
# so a wrong value means the browser blocks every product image with nothing in
# any server log. Changing it needs a rebuild, not a restart.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MEDIA_URL=https://pub-<32 hex>.r2.dev
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MEDIA_URL=https://cdn.edawr.in

# ---- Site URL ----
# This storefront's own public origin. OPTIONAL; defaults to https://edawr.in.
#
# Only used to make `og:image` and `twitter:image` absolute — social crawlers
# cannot resolve a relative one. Set it on a preview deployment so its cards
# point at itself rather than at production.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://edawr.in
